  "description": [],
  "history": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Origin",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "On one day of extraordinary intelligence, Taravangian worked out the likely course of events and a plan to save humanity from the Desolation. He wrote it over the walls and furniture of his bedroom; the copied writings are the Diagram.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Taravangian knew of Gavilar's visions of the coming storm and asked the Nightwatcher for the capacity to save Roshar. Since then his intelligence and compassion change daily, one high when the other is low.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
        }
      ],
      "parts": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Activities",
      "items": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Interpreting the Diagram",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Senior members spend much of their time interpreting it. Written in codes, drawings, poetry and invented languages, it often has to be put into plain speech first, and members disagree over what it calls for.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "On a brilliant day, Taravangian cuts a copy of the Diagram to pieces to rework it.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-5" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Mrall, Adrotagia and Dukar debate whether the Diagram is still accurate.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Testing the King",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Taravangian takes a written test each day. Its result, judged by the King's Testers under Dukar, decides what he may do that day: comment on the Diagram, see people unsupervised, change policy or pass judgement.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Adrotagia's figures show another day of brilliance like his is unlikely more than once in two thousand years.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Taravangian has cheated on the test, pretending he couldn't solve a problem so he wouldn't be restricted for scoring too well.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Silent Gatherers",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "endnote" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Taravangian has dying hospital patients bled slowly so their last words, the Death Rattles, can be recorded. Those who do it are the Silent Gatherers, led by Joshor.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "endnote" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "The Death Rattles fall to two or fewer a day. Moelach settles in the Horneater Peaks, and Joshor heads there hoping to restore them.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Search for Dustbringers",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "The Diagram predicts the Dustbringers are the order most likely to ally with it, so lower members try to bond ashspren. Malata is the first to succeed.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "107" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Assassinations",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-6" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "78" }
                  ]
                },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "80" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "One of Taravangian's men holds Szeth's Oathstone and orders him to kill rulers across Roshar.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-6" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "78" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Szeth's last target is Dalinar, whose uniting of the highprinces Taravangian sees as a threat to the Diagram's aim that Taravangian rule Roshar.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "80" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Takeover of Jah Keved",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Szeth kills the Veden king and several highprinces, and the rest die in the civil war that follows. As the Diagram instructs, Taravangian arrives in Vedenar as a foreign king bringing aid, with a forged claim to the throne.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Highprince Valam names Taravangian his heir outright. That, seven factions where the Diagram predicted six, and Szeth's news of his fight with Kaladin make Taravangian doubt the Diagram.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-14" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Graves's conspiracy",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "84" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "43" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Graves, an Alethi Shardbearer, reads the Diagram as saying they must ally with Dalinar by making him king, so Elhokar must die. He, Moash, Rill and others try to make Elhokar fall from a balcony; Elhokar holds on and is saved.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Graves tries to recruit Kaladin, who refuses. When the plotters attack Elhokar directly, Kaladin saves him.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "84" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Graves says the Diagram spoke of the Radiants returning, but they didn't understand it in time.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "84" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Fleeing across the Frostlands with Moash, Graves is killed by Fused; Moash survives.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "43" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Second attempt on Dalinar",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "85" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "86" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "On the Diagram's orders, Graves keeps Kaladin away from Dalinar so Szeth won't learn the Radiants have returned.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Szeth attacks Dalinar at Narak; Roion and others die defending him, and Szeth Lashes Dalinar into the sky.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "85" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Kaladin catches Dalinar and defeats Szeth.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "86" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Undermining Dalinar",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-5" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Taravangian, first ruler to join Dalinar's coalition, decides on a brilliant day that Dalinar should be replaced as its leader.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-5" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "They release secrets together to turn people against Dalinar, among them that Elhokar swore to him as highking and that he hid visions in which he spoke with Odium.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Thaylen Field",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "During the battle, Malata opens the Veden Oathgate for singers to attack Urithiru, and a Diagram agent steals Jezrien's Honorblade.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Alliance with Odium",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "On a day of low intelligence, Odium confronts Taravangian, as the Diagram predicted. Taravangian allies the Diagram with Odium in exchange for the safety of everyone born in Kharbranth and their spouses, and gives Odium's forces the Honorblade.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "122" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Disbanding",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-3" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A year after Thaylen Field, Taravangian disbands the Diagram before his armies betray the coalition in Emul. Members who know too much are to be sent on long secret quests rather than released.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-3" }]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
